WEBVTT

00:09:28.522 --> 00:09:30.858
it addresses a problem
that we already had,

00:09:30.899 --> 00:09:32.901
a conflict between theory and experiment

00:09:32.943 --> 00:09:34.820
in the realm of quark physics.

00:09:36.030 --> 00:09:39.116
"OK," you say, "but, like,
how can I visualize it?"

00:09:39.158 --> 00:09:42.036
At this point in the talk,
you should know better, right?

00:09:42.077 --> 00:09:44.830
Because to first approximation,
dark matter is invisible.

00:09:45.122 --> 00:09:46.206
(Laughter)

00:09:46.248 --> 00:09:48.125
But I know you really want a visual,

00:09:48.125 --> 00:09:49.793
so I'm going to give you one.

00:09:50.544 --> 00:09:53.047
Here's what it looks like to me,
in my everyday work.

00:09:53.088 --> 00:09:54.465
(Laughter)

00:09:54.506 --> 00:09:58.552
(Applause)

00:09:58.594 --> 00:10:02.222
Which is to say,
it's OK if this is unintuitive.